messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA committee works for two years and is composed of 4 members each year, 2 of which are from the following 4 judges: F, G, H and I, and the other 2 members are from the following 3 scientists: V, Y and Z. Each year, the committee is chaired by one member. A member who chairs the first year must retire from the committee during the second year. The person who chairs the second year must be a member of the committee during the first year. The committee members must meet the following conditions: G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year. H and Y cannot be members of this committee in the same year. Each year, only one of I and V is a member of this committee.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if H is the chairman in the first year, which of the followings can be the chairman in the second year?\n# Options:\nA) F\nB) G\nC) Y\nD) I', "<think>.\nTo solve this problem, we need to carefully analyze the given conditions and constraints. Let's break it down step by step:.\n\n1. **Committee Composition and Conditions:**.\n   - The committee consists of 4 members each year.\n   - 2 judges (F, G, H, I) and 2 scientists (V, Y, Z).\n   - G and V cannot be in the same year.\n   - H and Y cannot be in the same year.\n   - Only one of I and V can be in the committee each year.\n   - The chairman must be a member of the committee in the first year and must be a different member in the second year.\n\n2. **Given Information:**.\n   - H is the chairman in the first year.\n   - H and Y cannot be in the same year, so Y cannot be in the first year.\n   - G and V cannot be in the same year, so if G is in the first year, V cannot be in the first year.\n   - Only one of I and V can be in the committee each year.\n\n3. **First Year Committee:**.\n   - H is the chairman.\n   - Since H is in the first year, Y cannot be in the first year.\n   - Only one of I and V can be in the first year.\n   - Therefore, the first year committee must be: H, I, V, or H, I, Y, or H, I, Z (but Y and Z are not available).\n\n4. **Second Year Committee:**.\n   - The second year chairman must be a member of the first year committee.\n   - The second year chairman cannot be H (since H is the first year chairman).\n   - The second year chairman must be one of the members of the first year committee.\n\n5. **Possible First Year Combinations:**.\n   - If I is in the first year, the committee is: H, I, V, Y (not possible since Y is not available).\n   - If V is in the first year, the committee is: H, V, I, Y (not possible since Y is not available).\n   - Therefore, the only possible first year committee is: H, I, V, Z.\n\n6. **Second Year Chairman:**.\n   - The second year chairman must be one of the members of the first year committee: H, I, V, Z.\n   - Since H is the first year chairman, H cannot be the second year chairman.\n   - Therefore, the second year chairman must be one of I, V, or Z.\n\n7. **Valid Options:**.\n   - F (not in the first year committee).\n   - G (not in the first year committee).\n   - Y (not in the first year committee).\n   - I (in the first year committee).\n\nThus, the only valid option for the second year chairman is I.\n\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
