specify that all new trees will absorb more carbon dioxide than the current average.\n   - Therefore, this statement is not strongly supported by the given information.\n\n4. **Option C:**\n   - This option states that the city will have 1000 new trees planted.\n   - The context does not provide any information about the number of new trees planted.\n   - Therefore, this statement is not strongly supported by the given information.\n\n5. **Option D:**\n   - This option states that the city will have 1000 trees of the new type.\n   - The context only mentions that the new trees will be of a specific type, but it does not specify that all new trees will be of the new type.\n   - Therefore, this statement is not strongly supported by the given information.\n\nAfter analyzing each option, it is clear that the statement most strongly supported by the given information is:\n\n<answer>\nA) The city will have 1500 trees after the policy is implemented.\n</answer>\n</think>",
