:** "Parents think that children\'s failure to report information is more worrying than lying."\n     - The context does not explicitly state that parents think concealing information is more worrying than lying. It only mentions that concealing information is worse solved and not given enough attention.\n     - Therefore, this option is not supported by the text.\n   - **Option B:** "Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem."\n     - The context does not provide information about parents\' beliefs regarding the severity of lying as a moral problem. It only mentions that lying is a significant concern.\n     - Therefore, this option is not supported by the text.\n   - **Option C:** "Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying."\n     - The context states that many parents have not solved the problem of lying well, implying that they are not willing to solve it.\n     - Therefore, this option is not supported by the text.\n   - **Option D:** "Children\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents."\n     - The context explicitly states that the problem of children concealing their own situation is worse solved and not given enough attention.\n     - Therefore, this option is supported by the text.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is:\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
