messages:   35%|###4      | 208/600 [11:18<03:04,  2.12it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nDirect selling refers to the business mode in which direct selling enterprises recruit sellers to sell products directly to final consumers outside the fixed business place.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is direct selling?\n# Options:\nA) After selecting salesmen, a dairy manufacturer set up 100 sales points in the city to sell dairy products at a unified price.\nB) A bookstore adopts online sales. after customers place an order, the courier will send the products to the designated place and charge a fee.\nC) Some salesmen recruited by a cosmetics brand set up stalls along the road to distribute product descriptions and sell them to customers at lower prices.\nD) At the beginning of school, the new student xiao he bought five table lamps in the wholesale market, one for his own use, and the other four were sold to his classmates.', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to understand the definition of direct selling provided in the context. Direct selling is a business mode where direct selling enterprises recruit sellers to sell products directly to final consumers outside the fixed business place. This means that in direct selling, the sales are made directly to the consumers without going through a traditional retail channel.\n\nLet's analyze each option based on this definition:.\n\nA) After selecting salesmen, a dairy manufacturer set up 100 sales points in the city to sell dairy products at a unified price.\n- This option describes a scenario where the dairy manufacturer sets up sales points (fixed business places) to sell products. This is not direct selling because the sales are made through these fixed business places, not directly to the consumers.\n\nB) A bookstore adopts online sales. After customers place an order, the courier will send the products to the designated place and charge a fee.\n- This option describes an online sales model where the bookstore uses an online platform to sell products. The products are delivered to the customers, but the sales are still made through the online platform, not directly to the consumers. This is not direct selling.\n\nC) Some salesmen recruited by a cosmetics brand set up stalls along the road to distribute product descriptions and sell them to customers at lower prices.\n- This option describes a scenario where salesmen are directly selling products to consumers at stalls along the road. This matches the definition of direct selling because the sales are made directly to the consumers outside the fixed business place. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
