messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnalogical argument is based on the sameness or similarity of two objects in some attributes, and infers that the two objects are also the same or similar in other attributes. Its logical form is that object A has the attributes of a, b, c and d. Object B has properties of a, b, c. So object B has the property of d.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the followings belongs to analogical argument?\n# Options:\nA) Tao yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, li bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. this shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries\nB) Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation\nC) Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, comrade bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that comrade bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others\nD) Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper', '<think>.\nTo solve this problem, we need to identify which option fits the definition of an analogical argument. According to the definition provided, an analogical argument compares two objects based on their similarities in certain attributes and infers that they are also similar in other attributes.\n\nLet\'s analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) "Tao Yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, Li Bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. This shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries.".\n- This statement is making a comparison between Tao Yuanming and Li Bai based on their behavior towards power and status. It does not compare two objects based on attributes and infer similarity in other attributes. This is more of a moral or ethical comparison.\n\nB) "Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction, and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation.".\n- This statement is comparing light and sound based on their common phenomena (linear propagation, refraction, and reflection). It then infers that light, like sound, also has a specific attribute (fluctuation). This fits the definition of an analogical argument.\n\nC) "Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, Comrade Bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that Comrade Bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others.".\n- This statement is making a comparison between Comrade Bethune and others based on their work ethic and dedication. It does not compare two objects based on attributes and infer similarity in other attributes. This is more of a descriptive comparison.\n\nD) "Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper.".\n- This statement is comparing silver and copper based on their electrical conductivity and resistivity. It then infers that silver is more suitable for conductive materials based on this comparison. This also fits the definition of an analogical argument.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, we can see that options B and D both fit the definition of an analogical argument. However, the question asks for the option that "belongs to" the analogical argument, implying a single correct answer. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
