pays more for internet advertising than for television advertising.\n- This option suggests that the firm spends more on Internet advertisements. However, if the firm spends more on Internet advertisements, it would likely generate less revenue from them, not more. Therefore, this option does not resolve the paradox.\n\nD) Internet advertisements allow the firm to more accurately target audiences.\n- This option suggests that Internet advertisements are more effective in reaching the intended audience. Given that the audience for television advertisements is one thousand times larger than the Internet audience, and the firm generates two-thirds of its revenue from Internet advertisements, it implies that the Internet advertisements are more efficient in terms of reaching the target audience. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
