messages:   48%|####7     | 285/600 [11:46<01:45,  2.99it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nBroken window effect is a psychological phenomenon, that is, if the window of a house is broken and no one repair it, and soon other windows will also be broken.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which one of the followings does not belong to broken window effect?\n# Options:\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\nD) If a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, many people will soon speak uncivilized languages.', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to understand the broken window effect and apply it to each option. The broken window effect suggests that if a small problem (like a broken window) is not addressed, it will lead to more problems (like more broken windows).\n\nLet's analyze each option:.\n\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\n- This fits the broken window effect. If graffiti is not cleaned, it will likely lead to more graffiti being added to the wall.\n\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\n- This also fits the broken window effect. If pollution is not treated, it can spread and affect the entire basin.\n\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\n- This does not fit the broken window effect. The presence of rubbish in a clean place does not lead to more rubbish being thrown away. Instead, it might lead to more people feeling ashamed and trying to clean up. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
