messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAggression behavior is short for aggression, sometimes it can also be called aggression. It refers to the behavior of individuals who violate the mainstream norms of society, have motivation and hurt others.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following violations belongs to aggression behavior\n# Options:\nA) A doctoral student at a university in california broke into his office and wounded his mentor with a gun\nB) A middle school chinese teacher criticized the students who did not finish their summer homework on time\nC) In an ice hockey game, party a's players accidentally hit party b's players in the process of grabbing the ball\nD) With li's consent, wang sent li's sick photos to the wechat's circles ", "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the definition of aggression behavior provided in the context and then evaluate each option to see which one fits the definition.\n\nThe definition of aggression behavior is:.\n1. It refers to the behavior of individuals.\n2. This behavior violates the mainstream norms of society.\n3. It has a motivation.\n4. It involves hurting others.\n\nLet's analyze each option based on these criteria:.\n\nA) A doctoral student at a university in California broke into his office and wounded his mentor with a gun.\n- This behavior involves a violation of societal norms (breaking into someone's office).\n- It has a clear motivation (to hurt the mentor).\n- It involves hurting others (wounding the mentor).\n- This fits all the criteria of aggression behavior.\n\nB) A middle school Chinese teacher criticized students who did not finish their summer homework on time.\n- This behavior involves a violation of societal norms (criticizing students for not completing homework).\n- However, it does not have a clear motivation to hurt others.\n- This does not fit the definition of aggression behavior.\n\nC) In an ice hockey game, party A's players accidentally hit party B's players in the process of grabbing the ball.\n- This behavior involves a violation of societal norms (hitting players during a game).\n- However, it is accidental and not intentional.\n- This does not fit the definition of aggression behavior.\n\nD) With Li's consent, Wang sent Li's sick photos to the WeChat's circles.\n- This behavior involves a violation of societal norms (sharing private information without consent).\n- However, it does not have a clear motivation to hurt others.\n- This does not fit the definition of aggression behavior. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
