retation.\n   - **Option B: A reader's enjoyment of a poem is enhanced by knowing the poet's interpretation of it.**.\n     - This is also possible. Knowing the poet's interpretation can provide additional context and insight, potentially enhancing the reader's enjoyment.\n   - **Option C: A modern reader and a nineteenth-century reader interpret one of Shakespeare's sonnets in the same way.**.\n     - This is the option we need to evaluate carefully. The critic states that any two readers from different cultures or eras have radically different systems of beliefs. Since Shakespeare's sonnets are from the 16th and 17th centuries, a modern reader and a nineteenth-century reader (which is close to the 17th century) would indeed have radically different systems of beliefs. Therefore, it is highly unlikely that they would interpret the sonnets in the same way.\n   - **Option D: A reader's interpretation of a poem evolves over time.**.\n     - This is possible. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
