messages:   62%|######1   | 369/600 [20:51<03:34,  1.08it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNucleic acids and other genetic foods that appear in the name of health care products are not very helpful to human health. From a scientific point of view, the so-called human body needs to be supplemented with exogenous nucleic acids cannot be established. What the human body lacks is nutrition, and nucleic acid cannot be lacking. Some advertisements say that when people are old or sick, their ability to make genes will be weakened, which is even more nonsense.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options can be inferred?\n# Options:\nA) All advertisements about health products lack scientific basis.\nB) Nucleic acid in the human body will decrease with age.\nC) Illness is the result of malnutrition.\nD) Eating health products may not promote your health.', "<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the context and analyze each option step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis:**\n   - The context states that nucleic acids and other genetic foods in health care products are not very helpful to human health.\n   - It mentions that the claim of needing exogenous nucleic acids is scientifically unfounded.\n   - The context also states that the human body lacks nutrition, not nucleic acid.\n   - It further clarifies that the advertisement suggesting that gene-making ability weakens with age is incorrect.\n\n2. **Option Analysis:**\n   - **Option A: All advertisements about health products lack scientific basis.**\n     - The context does not explicitly state that all advertisements lack scientific basis. It only mentions that specific claims about nucleic acids are unfounded. Therefore, this option cannot be definitively inferred.\n   - **Option B: Nucleic acid in the human body will 