 Establishing that experience teaches us the opposite of what lance concludes**.\n     - Frank does not argue that experience teaches the opposite. He is using the assumption of Lance\'s conclusion to derive a contradiction.\n   - **Option C: Showing that lance\'s conclusion involves him in a contradiction**.\n     - This is the correct option. Frank\'s argument is based on the assumption that Lance\'s conclusion is true. If Lance\'s conclusion is true, then there must be at least one general rule with no exceptions. This directly contradicts Lance\'s own statement that every general rule has at least one exception.\n   - **Option D: Showing that it has no implications for any real cases**.\n     - Frank\'s argument does have implications for real cases. It shows that if Lance\'s conclusion is true, then there must be at least one real case where a general rule has no exceptions.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**.\n   - Frank\'s argument is an attempt to counter Lance\'s conclusion by showing that if Lance\'s conclusion is true, it leads to a contradiction. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
