W cannot be in the production department.\n- Therefore, G can be assigned to the sales department without violating any conditions.\n\n**Option B: H is assigned to the production department.**\n- If X and F are in the sales department, W must be in the production department (Condition 3).\n- Since F is in the production department (Condition 4), W cannot be in the production department.\n- Therefore, H can be assigned to the production department without violating any conditions.\n\n**Option C: I was assigned to the sales department.**\n- If X and F are in the sales department, W must be in the production department (Condition 3).\n- Since F is in the production department (Condition 4), W cannot be in the production department.\n- Therefore, I can be assigned to the sales department without violating any conditions.\n\n**Option D: W was assigned to the public relations department.**\n- If X and F are in the sales department, W must be in the production department (Condition 3).\n- Since F is in the production department (Condition 4), W cannot be in the production department.\n- Therefore, W cannot be assigned to the public relations department if X and F are in the sales department.\n\nFrom the analysis, we can see that the statement that cannot be true if X and F are assigned to the same department is:\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
