most diligent people cannot read all the books, then the most diligent person cannot read all the books either. Therefore, this option is incorrect.\n   - **Option D:** "People who read all the books in the world must be the most diligent people in the world.".\n     - This option is also incorrect. The context does not provide any information about people who read all the books being the most diligent people. It only states that the most diligent people cannot read all the books.\n\n3. **Conclusion:**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
