e equal, or the number of girls could be more than the number of boys.\n   - **Option C:** "The total number of boys in the liberal arts class is higher than that of girls in the science class."\n     - This option is not necessarily true. We do not have any information about the number of boys and girls in the science class relative to the liberal arts class.\n   - **Option D:** "The total number of boys in the science class is more than that of girls in the liberal arts class."\n     - This option is the only one that can be definitively concluded based on the given information.\n     - Since there are more science classes than liberal arts classes, and there are more boys than girls in the high school, it follows that there must be more boys in the science classes than in the liberal arts classes. This is because the total number of boys exceeds the total number of girls, and the science classes are a subset of the total classes.\n\nTherefore, the correct option is:\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
