messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is closest to the meaning of the above judgement?\n# Options:\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nC) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\nD) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given context and analyze each option step by step.\n\nThe context states: "If you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.".\n\nThis statement can be rephrased in a more formal logical form:.\n- If P (closing all the wrong doors), then Q (truth will be shut out).\n\nWe need to find the option that best captures the meaning of this statement.\n\nLet\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\n- This option suggests a conditional statement: If Q (truth is shut out), then P (you close all the wrong doors).\n- This is the contrapositive of the original statement, but it does not directly capture the original meaning.\n\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\n- This option suggests that for truth not to be shut out, all the wrong doors must be closed.\n- This is the contrapositive of the original statement, which means it captures the original meaning.\n\nC) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\n- This option suggests that if truth is not shut out, then not all wrong doors are closed.\n- This is not the contrapositive and does not directly capture the original meaning.\n\nD) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.\n- This option suggests a different logical relationship: Rejecting wrong leads to accepting truth.\n- This is not directly related to the original statement. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
