messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nRural culture is a set of contextual production and life experience system, which is determined by the production and living conditions of the society. in any case, the import of advanced culture from the outside to such a society is divorced from reality.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the most accurate understanding of the meaning of contextual in this paragraph?\n# Options:\nA) Adapted to the experience of production and life in various parts of the countryside\nB) Adapting to the actual development and changes in rural areas\nC) Connected with and integrated with the reality of the local rural society\nD) Adapted to the development of advanced culture', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the context and the question. The context provides information about rural culture being a system determined by the production and living conditions of the society. It also mentions that the import of advanced culture from the outside is divorced from reality. This implies that the culture must be in harmony with the local reality.\n\nLet\'s break down each option:.\n\nA) Adapted to the experience of production and life in various parts of the countryside.\n- This option suggests that the culture is adapted to the general experiences in rural areas. While this is true, it does not specifically emphasize the integration with the local reality.\n\nB) Adapting to the actual development and changes in rural areas.\n- This option focuses on adapting to the development and changes in rural areas. However, it does not directly address the integration with the local reality.\n\nC) Connected with and integrated with the reality of the local rural society.\n- This option directly addresses the idea that the culture must be in harmony with the local reality. It emphasizes the integration and connection with the local context.\n\nD) Adapted to the development of advanced culture.\n- This option suggests that the culture is adapted to the development of advanced culture. However, it does not specifically mention the local reality or integration.\n\nGiven the context, the most accurate understanding of the meaning of "contextual" in this paragraph is the one that emphasizes the integration with the local reality. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
