escribes a preventive measure to reduce pollution. It demonstrates a commitment to environmental protection and reducing negative impacts on the community. This also aligns with the definition of corporate social response.\n\nC) An enterprise donated 300 million enterprise shares to charity organizations to set up a special fund.\n- This option involves a financial contribution to support charitable causes. While this can be seen as a positive action, it does not necessarily align with the definition of corporate social response. The context emphasizes actions that directly address societal needs or ethical standards, rather than just financial contributions. Therefore, this option may not fully meet the criteria of corporate social response.\n\nD) A company arranges employment for the disabled in accordance with the provisions of the law on the protection of the disabled.\n- This option involves a legal requirement to provide employment opportunities for the disabled. It ensures compliance with legal standards and promotes inclusivity, which is a societal need. This aligns with the definition of corporate social response. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
