ay not be able to present themselves effectively or match the job requirements. This lack of familiarity could be a significant barrier to employment.\n\nC) **The actual salary levels of most returnees do not meet their expectations.**.\n   - While this might contribute to the difficulty in finding employment, it does not directly explain why returnees are having trouble. It focuses on salary expectations rather than the broader context of employment.\n\nD) **Graduates of famous overseas universities such as oxford are still favored by employers.**.\n   - This option suggests that employers still prefer graduates from prestigious universities. However, it does not explain why returnees from other universities are having difficulty finding employment. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
