messages:   95%|#########5| 571/600 [27:30<00:04,  6.87it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSome TV ads take the same words, repeated many times in order to deepen the audience's impression, so that the audience remember the product to be promoted. In fact, this is unwise.Surveys show that many long-term such advertising businesses. Lately, they've been in economic trouble, with a huge backlog of products. It can be seen that the business not only did not achieve the desired purpose, but also produced a negative effect.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options best emphasizes the above argument?\n# Options:\nA) Although some tv viewers don't care about the same ad being repeated, many viewers feel it's best to take more of the art of advertising into account\nB) Because the audience is with a good tv program after watching an ad, any ad will make the audience impatient\nC) Although the advertising act does not prohibit the same ad word repeatedly, merchants should consider the diverse feelings of different audiences\nD) Repeated playback of the same ad will cause tv viewers to get bored or even angry, and thus have a strong antipathy to the products that the merchant is trying to promote", '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the context and the question. The context provides information about the effectiveness of repetitive TV ads and their negative impact on businesses. The question asks us to identify the option that best emphasizes this argument.\n\nLet\'s break down the context:.\n1. TV ads use the same words repeatedly to create a strong impression.\n2. This strategy is not effective and has led to economic troubles for many businesses.\n3. The argument is that this approach did not achieve the desired effect and had a negative impact.\n\nNow, let\'s examine each option:.\n\nA) "Although some tv viewers don\'t care about the same ad being repeated, many viewers feel it\'s best to take more of the art of advertising into account.".\n- This option introduces a contrast between viewers who don\'t care about repetition and those who do. It does not directly address the negative impact of repetitive ads or the argument that the strategy did not achieve the desired effect.\n\nB) "Because the audience is with a good tv program after watching an ad, any ad will make the audience impatient.".\n- This option suggests that the audience becomes impatient after watching an ad, but it does not directly address the negative impact of repetitive ads or the argument that the strategy did not achieve the desired effect.\n\nC) "Although the advertising act does not prohibit the same ad word repeatedly, merchants should consider the diverse feelings of different audiences.".\n- This option acknowledges that repetition is allowed but suggests that merchants should consider the audience\'s diverse feelings. While it touches on the idea of audience diversity, it does not emphasize the negative impact of repetitive ads or the argument that the strategy did not achieve the desired effect.\n\nD) "Repeated playback of the same ad will cause tv viewers to get bored or even angry, and thus have a strong antipathy to the products that the merchant is trying to promote.".\n- This option directly addresses the negative impact of repetitive ads. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
