ation where two substances (saccharin and sodium glutamate) are present together, and their combined effect on taste is less than the sum of their individual effects. This also fits the definition of antagonism.\n\nC) After taking sodium chloride and quinine at the same time, drinking water will have a slightly sweet feeling.\n- This option describes a situation where two substances (sodium chloride and quinine) are present together, and their combined effect on taste is less than the sum of their individual effects. This fits the definition of antagonism.\n\nD) After eating sour sambal, and then eating sour food, you will not taste the sour taste. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
